node_modules/
web/.next/
web/out/
.vercel/

# OS
.DS_Store
web/node_modules
web/.next
web/out
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
# Generated publication artifacts are NOW COMMITTED, deliberately.
#
# They are rebuilt by `make artifacts` from the accepted pipeline outputs, and by the
# Phase 6 gate before it runs the acceptance tests, so a developer clone still reproduces
# them rather than trusting the committed copy. But reproducing them requires the
# git-ignored 4.4 GB source cache, which a deployment build host does not have and must
# not need.
#
# Ignoring them meant a clean clone contained zero files under web/public/, so a static
# host would build successfully and serve an application whose every data fetch 404s. The
# whole set is 11 MB across 10 files, largest 7.1 MB - comfortably inside Git and host
# limits - so versioning them with the release is simpler and more reliable than staging
# them through object storage, and it keeps the deployed site byte-identical to the
# artifacts the gate verified.
#
# See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md for the reasoning and the alternative that was rejected.
